# Errors and notices of Folders' connections to servers and phones: the shared error words, address reading, and names a server sent that cannot be shown.

folders-remote-mod-heard-card = { $host } answers at { $at }, port { $port }. That address was only heard on the network, where any device can answer to a name, so the password has not been sent. If that is its address, press Connect.
folders-remote-mod-heard-stopped = { $host } answers at { $at }, an address that was only heard on the network, so the password has not been sent. Open { $host } again to check its address.
folders-remote-mod-bad-address = That address could not be read: { $why }.
folders-remote-mod-needs-password = This server needs a password or a key.
folders-remote-mod-login-refused = The server did not accept that login.
folders-remote-mod-host-key-unknown = { $host } has not been visited before, so its identity is unknown.
folders-remote-mod-host-key-changed = { $host } no longer has the identity it had before. It may have been rebuilt, or someone may be in the way.
folders-remote-mod-cert-unknown = { $host }'s certificate could not be checked: { $why }.
folders-remote-mod-cert-changed = { $host }'s certificate is not the one you trusted before.
folders-remote-mod-unreachable = Could not reach it: { $why }.
folders-remote-mod-not-found = { $what } is not there.
folders-remote-mod-exists = { $what } is already there.
folders-remote-mod-denied = Permission was refused for { $what }.
folders-remote-mod-busy = { $what } is in use by another program.
folders-remote-mod-not-supported = { $what } is not supported yet.
folders-remote-mod-cancelled = Cancelled.
folders-remote-mod-too-much = It sent far more than an answer can hold, so it was stopped.
folders-remote-mod-links = Links
folders-remote-mod-copy-share = Copying with a Windows share before it is opened
folders-remote-mod-copy-nfs = Copying with an NFS export before it is opened

folders-remote-address-no-scheme = it has no sftp://, ftp:// or mtp:// at the start
folders-remote-address-bad-scheme = only sftp://, ftp://, ftps://, ftpes://, dav://, davs://, smb://, nfs:// and mtp:// can be opened
folders-remote-address-no-bracket = a [ has no ]
folders-remote-address-no-server = it names no server
folders-remote-address-bad-name = the server's name is not one
folders-remote-address-line-break = the path holds a line break
folders-remote-address-after-name = there is something after the server's name
folders-remote-address-not-port = { $port } is not a port

folders-remote-screen-not-a-name = skipped: the server sent an unsafe name
folders-remote-screen-no-name = a thing with no name
